        "original_id": "0517f344-d9f7-5155-8b5d-330cc0394740",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Legends of the Fall; Legends of the Fall novella\n- People: Jim Harrison; Dorree Cooper\n- Places: Montana\n- Topics: American writing; Academy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Jim Harrison was born on December 11, 1937, and he became an American writer known for poetry, fiction, reviews, essays about the outdoors, and writings about food.\n- The 1979 novella Legends of the Fall was written by Jim Harrison.\n- The film Legends of the Fall is based on Jim Harrison’s 1979 novella of the same title.\n- The film Legends of the Fall is about three brothers and their father living in the wilderness and plains of Montana in the early 20th century, and about how nature, history, war, and love affect their lives.\n- Dorree Cooper was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Art Direction for the film Legends of the Fall.\n- Jim Harrison died on March 26, 2016.",
